            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00007-alt",
              "text": "Conversion of a carboxylic acid to an acid chloride, by reaction with thionyl chloride in trichloromethane (chloroform). The hydroxyl group is replaced by a chlorine atom."
