            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00011",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00011-alt",
              "text": "Hydrolysis of an acid chloride using water to give a carboxylic acid and hydrochloric acid."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_006.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00012",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00012-alt",
              "text": "Reaction of an acid chloride with a carboxylate in to form an acid anhydride."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_007.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00013",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00013-alt",
              "text": "The reaction of an acid chloride with an alcohol in the presence of pyridine to form an ester."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_008.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00014",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00014-alt",
              "text": "Two molecules of ammonia react with an acid chloride to form an amide and ammonium chloride."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_009.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00015",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00015-alt",
              "text": "Reaction of an acid chloride with lithium aluminum hydride in ether followed by treatment with acid to generate an alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_21_EC_010.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00016",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00248:alt:fig-00016-alt",
              "text": "Reaction of an acid chloride with two moles of Grignard reagent in ether followed by treatment with acid to give a tertiary alcohol."
